<!DOCTYPE score-partwise PUBLIC "-//Recordare//DTD MusicXML 4.0 Partwise//EN" "http://www.musicxml.org/dtds/partwise.dtd">
<!-- Hand-written for epiphany-musicxml's tests. Quarter-tone accidentals
     written as MuseScore writes them, by name with no <alter>: measures 1 to
     4 hold each of the fourteen names once. Each applies to its own note
     alone, as MuseScore reads it: in measure 5 one set by the second voice
     reaches no later note, neither the first voice's B, which the file
     writes earlier, nor one at another octave or on the other staff, and a
     natural follows it. In measures 6 to 9 an accidental carries over a tie,
     across the barline, to the tied note alone, and along a chain of two
     ties. In measures 10 and 11 two voices tie the same written D over a
     barline, one natural and one a quarter-tone sharp, and each continuation
     keeps its own. In measure 12 a note that writes no accidental, after two
     quarter-tone accidentals of different value on its line, is natural. -->
